removal is unplug-then-slide at the D2 door; arm pigtails up the side bands (|X| 50 to 55, Z 42 to 50, Y 160 to 353.6; 5 x 8 mm per side, tight); waist, aux, leg and charge pigtails down the same bands
to inline connectors below Y 190. **Gate 2 correction:** the earlier front-corner path (Z 62 to 70) ran through the front rails and 8 corner brackets, and the
"Z 50 to 60 gap" between the shelf and the shared front rail does not exist (the shelf ends at Z 50, the rail starts there). **There is no cable passage
from the lower box to the upper bay** today. Proposed: a 10 x 10 notch in each front corner of the printed shelf plate (|X| 45 to 55, Z 40 to 50), Joey's call. Only small
connectors on the LP bottom edge mate downward. The shelf plate stays as built (cutout idea withdrawn). Frame bonding: one point, at a carrier standoff, 1 M� ? 10 nF to system ground (board thread's
proposal, agreed: the frame touches the actuator housings anyway, so "floating" would not be). Connector edges: top = pack XT90 and
16-pin balance (rear face), both arm ports, USB to the Pi, fans; bottom = waist and leg ports, brake resistor; sides = E-stop loop,
charge port, sensors. On-pack BMS (Joey's pick, battery thread main d42e88f): a JK-BD6A17S8P, 133 x 81 x 18 with standoffs, sits on the pack's rear face at X -40.5 to 40.5, Y 186 to 319, Z -65 to -45, long axis along Y, FET heatsink facing rearward toward D2, 5 mm inside the frame rear face. The XT60 charge pigtail parks flat beside the XT90S (X -42 to -17, Y 325 to 345, Z -58 to -45). The sense board and its 2 x 10 connector are gone. All of it stays in |X| � 45, Z � -68 and slides out with the pack through D2. A Pi power stub (30 x 20 x 10, 12 V in from the logic board, 5 V out to the Pi's GPIO header; PLAN.md 6a, main e7d0b62)
sits on the compute shelf beside the Pi at X 22 to 52, Z 20 to 40, clear of the IMU. The FlexVolt options (D1 to D3) stay in `generator/variants.py` as the record of what was rejected.

Volumes: upper bay 156.8 x 100 x 101.4 between the RS03 rears; lower box 110 x 100 x 178.6 between the bottom rails and the shared rails; waist bay 150 x 140 x 40 below the frame.

| Component | Envelope | Where | Fits? |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Pi 5 + CAN HAT | 85 x 56 x 21 | upper bay, on the shelf, ports rear (D1 door) | yes, as built |
| Jetson Orin Nano dev kit | 103 x 90.5 x 35, +10 for its fan | upper bay, second shelf at Y 410, ports rear | **yes**, 30 mm left under the top rails. Needs a shelf bracket on the shelf rails or the posts |
| Third compute board / USB hub | up to 90 x 60 x 20 | none yet | **no**: the pack and boards fill the lower box; pelvis or over the Pi |
| Shoulder pitch RS03 x 2 | O99 x 57 | through the upper box sides | yes (0.5 mm per side to the 100 inner depth, as built) |
| Waist yaw RS03 | O99 x 57 | 40 mm waist bay | **no**, 23 mm short including the 6 mm adapter plate (motor Y 92 to 149). Hip stage: pocket the adapter, add the +70 waist section, or redesign the pelvis around Joey's fixed cell |
| Power + logic boards (BMS, fuse, contactor, DC-DC, CAN) | 100 x 150 x 24 on one carrier | in front of the pack, Z 37.5 to 61.5 | yes, 8.5 mm behind the frame front face; **but** the corner bracket heads on the lower post inner faces (X �46.5 to 51, Y 175 to 203 and 325 to 353) reach 3.5 mm into the board corners: board thread keep-out (gate 2) |
| Battery, 13S2P 21700 pack | 95 x 162 x 79 | lower box, \|X\| � 47.5, Y 183 to 345 | **yes** (locked 06:13Z); retention is **open** (gate 2: the D2 door is not a restraint) |
| M18 HD12 aux bay (handoff draft) | 168 x 98 x 112 | upper back cantilever | **no**: the shell back has 10 to 17 mm to the frame and the spine pads sit there. Recommend dropping it or moving it to the pelvis |
| Fans | 40 x 40 x 10 | 2 exhaust, provisionally in the D1 door plane (Y 430 to 470); 2 intakes in the lower front panel (Y 264 to 304, 193 to 233) | provisional. Gate 2: the lower box has **no exhaust** (the shared rails and the shelf close it off from the upper bay); proposed exit via the V1 side grilles, shell thread |
| Sensors | IMU fitted; cameras/mics in the head later | shelf; top rails | yes |
| Harness | two 12-14 AWG + CAN trunks | side bands of the lower box, shoulder runs at Y 447 to 457 stopping at \|X\| 52 and crossing behind the Jetson | partly: no lower-to-upper passage yet (shelf notch proposed) |

With the 13S2P pack (95 x 162 x 79) the lower box holds the pack and the boards without widening; the open items from gate 2
(pack retention, the lower-to-upper cable passage, lower-box exhaust, bracket-head keep-outs) are listed in `review/GATE2_REVIEW.md`.

## 7. What changes from the built frame

0. (Power) No frame geometry change. The 13S2P pack and the power and bus board live in the lower box on two printed tray rails and a printed board carrier; how the rails attach and retain the pack is open (gate 2).

1. Cut the four 340 mm posts into 198.6 (lower) + 121.4 (upper).
2. New rails: 2 x 226 shared step rails, 2 x 186 top rails, 2 x 100 shelf rails.
3. Move the top side rails and the shelf side rails out 38 mm per side (they become the upper box and step side rails).
4. Add four 3 mm 6061-T6 gusset plates (front and rear of each step corner), 9 x M5 each.
5. Add 16 corner brackets (32 total: 28 x 2028 + 4 x 2020 at the top inner-X corners).
